    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁπτέον</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπτομαι</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one must cling to</i> a
			thing, <i>bestow pains upon</i> it, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουσικῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					377a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				461
			</span></i>; <i>one must partake of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλακοῦντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					250
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.371
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.44
			</span></i>.</div>
